## Prior results (2026-09-24, pre-rebase working tree, same code minus the rebase)

A wider 12-scenario harness (scratchpad only, not retained) passed twice: the five above plus a
vol-down tap mid-scan, a tap during the load (caught by the final pre-exec check), a
mixed disk (broken default + good entry, then a UI-selected boot of the good entry into gen2),
no disk at all (settle cap 5 s, then menu/no-bootable-entry), pocketboot.drm_page_flips=4
(menu/lab, page-flip lab markers unchanged), a 15 s discovery timeout with a throttled disk
(menu/discovery-timeout, banner cleared once discovery finished), and a failed menu-initiated
boot (banner shown, list not stuck in "booting", second entry then booted). Screendumps of
each menu were inspected: "Boot failed" banner, "No bootable OS found / Connect USB to use
fastboot" empty state, held vol-down did not scroll the selection. Those artifacts were lost
with the session scratchpad; the committed harness reproduces the core five.

Measured then: gen1 starting-up -> Starting new kernel 593-669 ms over 3 runs (mean 640 ms over
6); Watcher::finish closing evdev fds cost 20-35 ms via synchronize_rcu per close, which is why
6add2e1 holds the fds open across kexec (loaded -> kexec dropped from ~60 ms to ~30 ms).

